# MQC — deferred work (post-Phase-7)

## Status

The 7-phase MQC security hardening pass (issues #1–#12 + #6a +
the encrypted-identity rewrite) is fully shipped on `master`.
This file is now the **residual**: items that were deliberately
deferred during the main pass and have no current owner.

For what shipped — commits, per-issue mapping, design rationale,
spec deltas — see:

- [`README-mqc-1-issues.md`](./README-mqc-1-issues.md) — status
  table mapping each reviewer issue to its closing commit.
- [`README-plans.md`](./README-plans.md) — per-issue analyses
  (the "why" behind each design decision).
- [`draft-page-mqc-protocol-00.md`](./draft-page-mqc-protocol-00.md)
  — spec, normative wire format and verification chain.
- `git log socket-level-wrapper-MQC/` — full commit history,
  including the cumulative diff of every Phase 1–7 change.

The original 1255-line orchestration plan (Phase ordering,
dependency graph, cutover sequence, verification milestones,
suggested commit boundaries) is preserved in git history at
commit `671f016e0` and earlier — recover it with
`git show 671f016e0^:socket-level-wrapper-MQC/mqc-master.plan`
if you need the historical narrative.

